# MEDIA #

During the football season, the  [LINK: (Crimson Tide Sports Network) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crimson_Tide_Sports_Network]  (CTSN) broadcasts multiple shows on gameday for most sports. The network includes more than 60 radio stations across the country. Radio stations  [LINK: (WFFN) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/WFFN] -FM,  [LINK: (WTSK) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/WTSK] -AM as a backup, broadcast all home games in the Tuscaloosa area. [LINK: ([93]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alabama_Crimson_Tide_football#cite_note-95]

Football radio broadcasts begin three hours prior to the game's designated kickoff time with Chris Stewart and Tyler Watts in Around the SEC. [LINK: ([94]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alabama_Crimson_Tide_football#cite_note-Game-broadcasts-96]  The radio broadcast then moves to the Crimson Tide Tailgate Party hosted by Tom Roberts. [LINK: ([94]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alabama_Crimson_Tide_football#cite_note-Game-broadcasts-96]  Immediately following the end of the game, the Fifth Quarter Show begins as host Eli Gold talks to coaches and players and gives game statistics. [LINK: ([94]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alabama_Crimson_Tide_football#cite_note-Game-broadcasts-96]  For the 2008 season, former Alabama players and personalities were brought on to provide guest commentary for each broadcast. [LINK: ([95]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alabama_Crimson_Tide_football#cite_note-97]

Current radio staff: [LINK: ([96]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alabama_Crimson_Tide_football#cite_note-98]  [LINK: ([97]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alabama_Crimson_Tide_football#cite_note-99]

Chris Stewart – play-by-play

Tyler Watts – color analyst

[LINK: (Cory Reamer) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cory_Reamer]  – sideline reporter

Chris Stewart, Tyler Watts – pre- and post-game show co-host

Tom Roberts – director of broadcasting

Tom Stipe, Butch Owens, Brian Roberts – producers

